#!/usr/bin/env bash
# P-SAFE-03 and P-ATTR-01, THE FROZEN RENDER BLOCKS (T-0237, rv2-t0237 B1-B3). Sourced by BOTH
# ops/lib/check-safety-disclaimer and ops/lib/check-map-attribution and run LAST in each; it uses the caller's `fail`.
#
# Round 2 of PR #133 hid the conditions line and the credit at the COLLAPSED detent three ways, each green on every
# anchor both checks had: B1 moved `summary()` under HomeSheet's `if detent == .medium {`; B2 put
# `.opacity(sheetDetent == .collapsed ? 0 : 1)` on the `conditions` view; B3 laid an `.overlay` over the screen's
# ZStack after the approved mount. Chasing spellings buys a round per spelling (PR #101), so the blocks that draw
# the sheet, the line and the credit are FROZEN as whole-line WHITELISTS: ANY edit inside one is refused until its
# approved list below is edited in the same commit, deliberately (fail closed). An overlay over the sheet hides the
# conditions line (P-SAFE-03) as surely as the credit (P-ATTR-01), so both pins run every block.
#
# Each block is read from its declaration - a whole line that must occur exactly once in its file - to its
# matching close, by counting { and } on whole lines with no string state (a brace in a literal or a trailing
# comment is a changed line, refused anyway), and compared line by line with its approved list. Lines are
# trimmed, a trailing CR stripped, blank lines kept and compared; only a line whose trimmed text STARTS with //
# is dropped. Two fences around each block, both whitelists:
#   ABOVE      the first non-blank kept line above the declaration is the approved one (an `}` or an import): an
#              attribute there - a result builder, which may rewrite the whole block - is refused;
#   DIRECTIVES no kept line of the three files starts with `#`: an `#if` around a frozen block can compile an
#              unfrozen twin instead. The approved set is EMPTY; a `#Preview` added here is added below first.
#
# The blocks (a superset of the direction, ruled in T-0237's Log as R-rv2-2): HomeSheet.swift's whole struct;
# ScenicHomeScreen.swift's `public var body` (the ZStack and its whole modifier chain), `chips`, `sheetDetails`
# and `conditions`; the app shell's `struct ScenicDriveApp`. sheetSummary is frozen by -sheet's (s2).
#
# WHAT IT CANNOT SEE: whether any of it RENDERS - visible, hittable and not covered at BOTH detents is a runtime
# property, filed on T-0180 (main 558e154, its both-detents runtime clause); a modifier these blocks call
# (`.background`, `.overlay`) overloaded by an extension elsewhere in the module; what the views they name
# (DriveSelector, DriveDetails, AttributionFooter, GatedHandoffButton, SafetyDisclaimer) draw inside themselves;
# `/* */` comments.
